# Frontend Conventions

## Stack
- React SPA with Vite.
- TanStack Router route files live in `src/routes/`.
- Jotai holds multi-server session state in `serversAtom` (`src/state/servers.ts`).
- HTTP uses axios + axios-auth-refresh with per-server clients from `getServerClient(serverUrl)`.
- SharedWorker (`src/workers/shared-refresh-worker.ts`) coordinates refresh deduplication across tabs.

## Key Constraints
- Import shared contracts only via `@contracts/*`.
- Use `getServerClient(serverUrl)` for API calls; avoid ad-hoc axios instances in UI components.
- Refresh strategy is reactive (401 interceptor), not proactive timer-based.
- SharedWorker must deduplicate in-flight refresh per `serverUrl` for concurrent tabs.
- E2E uses Playwright with tests in `apps/frontend/e2e/`.

## Documentation
- Auth client architecture: `docs/auth/clients.md`
- Token and cookie policy: `docs/auth/tokens.md`
- Session refresh and SharedWorker: `docs/auth/sessions.md`
- Stack overview: `docs/STACK.md`

## Designer-to-frontend UI parity (chat shell)
- When implementing or migrating chat UI from `apps/designer`, preserve the accepted structural contract unless a product decision explicitly changes it.
- Required column structure for chat shell:
  - Flexbox-first (`flex flex-col`) per column.
  - Fixed header/footer via `shrink-0`.
  - Scrollable body via `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`.
- Avoid reintroducing page-level scrolling for the chat shell; keep scroll ownership inside column bodies.
- Preserve subtle incoming/outgoing message visual distinction and fixed message composer behavior in chat column.
- If frontend intentionally diverges from designer styling contract, update docs/rules in the same PR and explain the rationale.
